classDiagram
    class Provider {
        <<interface>>
        +Name() string
        +CreateCharge(ctx, req) (*ChargeResponse, error)
        +VerifyWebhook(payload, signature) (*WebhookEvent, error)
        +ParseEventMetadata(payload) (*EventMetadata, error)
        +GetTransaction(ctx, txID) (*Transaction, error)
    }
    
    class Refunder {
        <<interface>>
        +Refund(ctx, req) (*RefundResponse, error)
    }
    
    class StripeClient {
        -secretKey string
        -webhookSecret string
        -httpClient *http.Client
        +Name() "stripe"
        +CreateCharge() PaymentIntent API
        +VerifyWebhook() HMAC-SHA256 + timestamp
        +Refund() Stripe Refunds API
    }
    
    class ChapaClient {
        -secretKey string
        -httpClient *http.Client
        +Name() "chapa"
        +CreateCharge() Chapa Charge API
        +VerifyWebhook() Custom signature
        +GetTransaction() Chapa Verify API
    }
    
    class TelebirrClient {
        -appID string
        -appKey string
        -publicKey string
        -httpClient *http.Client
        +Name() "telebirr"
        +CreateCharge() Telebirr H5 API
        +VerifyWebhook() RSA signature
        +GetTransaction() Telebirr Query API
    }
    
    class Registry {
        -providers map[string]Provider
        +Register(p Provider)
        +Get(name string) (Provider, error)
    }
    
    class PaymentService {
        -registry *Registry
        -db *pgxpool.Pool
        -ledger *LedgerService
        -idempotency *IdempotencyStore
        +CreateIntent(merchantID, req)
    }
    
    Provider <|.. StripeClient : implements
    Provider <|.. ChapaClient : implements
    Provider <|.. TelebirrClient : implements
    Refunder <|.. StripeClient : implements
    
    Registry o-- Provider : contains
    PaymentService --> Registry : uses
    PaymentService --> Provider : calls via registry
    
    note for Provider "Strategy Pattern:\nBusiness logic depends on\nthis interface, not concrete\nimplementations.\n\nTo add M-Pesa or PayPal:\n1. Implement Provider\n2. Register in main()\n3. Zero changes to PaymentService"
    
    note for Registry "Open/Closed Principle:\nOpen for extension\n(add providers)\nClosed for modification\n(no core code changes)"
    
    note for StripeClient "Stripe Implementation:\n- Form-encoded POST\n- HTTP Basic Auth\n- HMAC-SHA256 webhooks\n- 5-minute timestamp skew\n- Idempotency-Key header"
    
    note for PaymentService "Service calls:\n1. registry.Get(provider)\n2. provider.CreateCharge(req)\n3. Normalizes response\n4. Never knows which provider"
